This folder contains programs that are useful in
setting up SiB4 simulations:
  -Global
  -Regional
  -Groups
  -Single Sites

A brief description of the files is listed below.
All the data used in these routines can be found on
Google Drive, in the directory:
>sib4_data/pre

-------------------
create_sibaero.f90
-------------------
Creates the parameter file for the aerodynamic constants 
   that are PFT-dependent.
Requires one input file:
  - Tables of the constants (AeroTab.nc)
Outputs the aerodynamic constants parameter file (sib_aero.nc)

-------------------
create_sibpft.f90
------------------
Creates a global map with SiB4 PFTs.
Requires two maps:
  - A PFT map, regridded to 0.5 degrees (pft35_global_0.5deg.nc)
  - A land mask, matching the 0.5 degrees (land_mask_0.5deg.nc)
Outputs the SiB4 PFT map (pftsib_global_0.5deg.nc)

----------------
create_sibvs.f90
----------------
Creates a new global SiB4 vegetation structure file.
Requires four input maps (expected to match):
  - Land mask (land_mask_0.5deg.nc)
  - PFT map (with SiB4 PFTs, pftsib_global_0.5deg.nc)
  - Soil sand/clay fraction map (soil_global_0.5deg.nc)
  - Soil reflectance map (soref_global_0.5deg.nc)
Outputs the SiB4 PFT/soil input file,
  which is used for global simulations (sib_vs_0.5deg.nc)

--------------------
regrid_pftfrac.f90
--------------------
Regrids 0.1-degree PFT data from MODIS 
  to dimensions specified in a land area map.
Requires two input files:
  - PFT map at finer resolution to combine/regrid (pft35_global_0.1.nc)
  - Land mask specifying the grid/map to create (land_mask_0.5deg.nc)
Outputs the regridded PFT map (pft35_global_0.5deg.nc)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
make_subdomain files
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
All these routines create the SiB4 input files necessary
  for non-global simulations.
All of the user input is set in the make_subdomain.txt file.
  - lat/lon specified region (subdomain option 1)
  - group of sites (subdomain option 2, list of sites)
  - single site (subdomain option 2, single site)


make_subdomain_sibdr_copy.f90
-------------------------------
Creates the driver data from existing single site data.
This routine only works (or is only useful) for 
  grouping single sites into a combined group
  which can then be run all at once.

make_subdomain_sibdr_new.f90
------------------------------
Creates the driver data from global data, typically MERRA.

make_subdomain_sibvs.f90
-------------------------
Creates the vegetation structure file (sib_vs).
For subdomains or groups, the output type will be a netcdf file.
For a single site, the output type will be a text file.


